# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPA fallback for Sanity-driven dynamic routes.
#
# A document published after the last build has no HTML file on the CDN, so
# Nitro's generated "/* /404.html 404" rule would answer before any JavaScript
# runs — and you cannot fetch your way out of a page that never loaded. These
# rules serve the app shell instead, letting Vue Router resolve the route and
# liveRefetch() pull the document straight from Sanity.
#
# Netlify serves an existing static file in preference to a redirect (there is
# no "!" force flag here), so every already-built page keeps serving its
# prerendered HTML with full OG tags. Only URLs with no file reach these rules.
#
# One prefix per dynamic page component in pages/:
#   /shop/*                    shop/[id].vue and shop/collections/[id].vue
#   /studio/collaborations/*   studio/collaborations/[id].vue
#   /studio/interiors/*        studio/interiors/[id].vue
#   /our-world/crafts/*        our-world/crafts/[id].vue
#   /news/latest/*             news/latest/[id].vue
#   /work/*                    work/[id].vue
#   /work-with-us/*            work-with-us/[id].vue
#   /info/*                    info/[id].vue
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: a catch-all for pages/[id].vue. That component matches
# any single-segment path, so a "/*" fallback would make EVERY mistyped URL on
# the site return 200 instead of 404. New top-level Sanity pages therefore
# still need a rebuild — a deliberate trade to keep real 404s working.
#
# KNOWN TRADE-OFF: an invalid URL under any prefix below now returns HTTP 200
# with a client-rendered error page rather than a real 404 (a "soft 404").
# Search engines treat those less favourably than a true 404.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/shop/*                   /200.html  200
/studio/collaborations/*  /200.html  200
/studio/interiors/*       /200.html  200
/our-world/crafts/*       /200.html  200
/news/latest/*            /200.html  200
/work/*                   /200.html  200
/work-with-us/*           /200.html  200
/info/*                   /200.html  200
